=== Revision Guidelines  ===
• Keep the heading and 5-paragraph structure.  Do not add additional sub-headings.
• Write in fluent, seamless English — paragraphs should flow naturally, avoiding formulaic or mechanical transitions. 
• Elaborate only where persuasive:
   - weave in unused facts or citations from ground.citations;  
   - add concise parentheticals for key authorities;  
   - tighten language.  
• Elaborate and enhance where useful, but keep the revised version ≤ 450 words **and each sentence ≤ 40 words**.  
• Vary transition words; avoid using “Accordingly” or “Therefore” more than **once** in the section.
• Retain the identical closing sentence requesting dismissal with prejudice; **do not duplicate it**.
• Bluebook citations: the first cite for any authority must be full (reporter pin, **court**, year).  For the principal controlling case(s), add **2–3 sentences** (facts, holding, analogy).  Other authorities may use a ≤ 15-word parenthetical.  When citing a non-binding case, introduce it with “See” or “See also” and include court and year; **never label it “persuasive.”**  Do not cite authorities beyond those provided
• **Order of authorities:** cite binding (Supreme Court, controlling circuit, state high court) before persuasive authority.  Use persuasive cases only where no binding case addresses the precise point.
• Introduce each case once in full; thereafter short-form or *Id.* Cite any given authority **no more than twice** (full + short). 
• Active voice, no filler words.  Every fact gets a Complaint pincite.

